{"extract": "Abraham ben Samuel Abulafia (Hebrew: אברהם בן שמואל אבולעפיה) was the founder of the school of \"Prophetic Kabbalah\". He was born in Zaragoza, Kingdom of Aragon, in 1240, and is assumed to have died sometime after 1291 following a stay on the island of Comino in the Maltese archipelago.", "links": [{"ns": 0, "title": "Comino", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Hebrew language", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Isidore Singer", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Kabbalah", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Kingdom of Aragon", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Maltese archipelago", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Public domain", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "The Jewish Encyclopedia", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Zaragoza", "exists": true}, {"ns": 4, "title": "Wikipedia:Citing sources", "exists": true}, {"ns": 4, "title": "Wikipedia:When to cite", "exists": true}, {"ns": 4, "title": "Wikipedia:WikiProject Reliability", "exists": true}, {"ns": 12, "title": "Help:Maintenance template removal", "exists": true}]}